// prism_ui_chart -- server-renderable chart components (prism/ui/, milestone MB.5): bar,
// sparkline (line), pie/share, gauge, legend. Every one is a COMPOSITION over the closed
// 22-primitive vocabulary (widget/), built through prism_ui_kit.nova and prism_structure.nova
// wherever they fit -- no new PrismNodeKind (axiom A7). None of the five depends on a canvas: bar
// is a `prism_grid` table, pie/legend are rows of `label`/`glyph`, gauge is a labelled `range`,
// sparkline is a `band` of glyphs -- the same vocabulary a text-mode bar chart tool uses, so both
// `prism_html_render` (a real `<table>` / `<input type=range>`) and `prism_ansi_render` (an
// aligned ASCII table / ASCII progress bar) already know how to draw every one of them without
// this file teaching either renderer anything new.
//
// ── WHY BAR IS BUILT ON prism_grid, NOT A HAND-STACKED band PER ROW ──────────────────────────
// A chart's bars must line up in a column -- label, bar, and value all starting at the same x
// position on every row. `band`/`stack` alone have no notion of a shared column width across
// SIBLING rows (each row's `band` sizes itself independently); `prism_structure.prism_grid` IS
// "tabular data" (PRISM_SPEC.md §10) and both backends already know how to align it: the ANSI
// renderer's `_ansi_grid` measures every column's widest cell and pads to it (reusing v0.1's
// `prism_ansi_table`), and the HTML renderer emits a real `<table>`. Composing on `prism_grid`
// gets column alignment in BOTH backends for free instead of re-deriving padding logic that
// `prism_ansi_table` already has. `key_fn = it.ch_item_label` also gives a duplicate series label
// `prism_grid`'s own "duplicate row key" rejection as a bonus (defense in depth) -- but
// `_prism_ch_check_items` below is still the check every caller actually hits first, because
// pie/legend do not route through grid/each at all and need it regardless.
//
// ── BAR WIDTH: A "TEXT-MODE BAR" IS A ROW OF check()/minus() GLYPHS, NOT A SIZED gap ────────────
// A `gap(size)` was considered and rejected for the same reason prism_ui_feedback.nova's progress
// rejected it: `gap` is LAYOUT SPACING (PRISM_SPEC.md §7), and the ANSI renderer emits a SINGLE
// space for a `gap` regardless of its `size` attr (prism_render_ansi.nova: `_ansi_gap` / the
// inline `"gap" => ok(" ")` arm) -- a gap-sized bar would be invisible on the one backend a
// text-mode bar chart most needs to work on. `prism_in_rating`'s own precedent
// (prism_ui_input.nova) already solved "the closed 12-icon set has no bar/block glyph" by reusing
// `Check()`/`Minus()` as filled/empty; this file reuses that exact precedent for a bar's cells.
// Width is an integer count of filled cells out of `PRISM_CH_BAR_TRACK`, computed as
// `(value * PRISM_CH_BAR_TRACK) / max_value` -- truncating integer division, guarded to 0 when
// `max_value == 0` (only possible when every value in the series is 0, since values are validated
// non-negative), so an all-zero series renders every bar fully empty instead of dividing by zero.
//
// ── GAUGE: WHY IT DOES NOT CALL prism_fb_progress DIRECTLY ───────────────────────────────────────
// `prism_fb_progress(label, done, total)` (prism_ui_feedback.nova) IS the "label + prism_range"
// idiom this component reuses -- but calling it as `prism_fb_progress(label, value - min_val,
// max_val - min_val)` would shift the underlying `range` node's own `min`/`max` attrs to `0` /
// `max_val - min_val` instead of the caller's REAL bounds. A gauge over, say, [32, 212] would then
// carry a `range` node reporting `min=0, max=180` -- correct arithmetic, wrong domain, and any
// caller reading those attrs back (a11y tooling, a test, a future DevTools inspector) would see a
// lie. `prism_ch_gauge` reuses the IDIOM (a percentage label above a `prism_range` track) but
// calls `prism_range` directly with the caller's own `min_val`/`max_val` -- the same "propagate,
// don't reimplement" discipline applied everywhere else in this file: `prism_range`'s own
// non-empty-label rejection is what actually rejects an empty label here, unchanged.
//
// ── PIE: LARGEST-REMAINDER APPORTIONMENT REUSES std/money/allocate.nova, NOT A NEW ALGORITHM ────
// "Percentages must sum to exactly 100" is precisely what std/money/allocate.nova's
// `alloc_weighted(minor, weights)` already guarantees (CLAUDE.md: does this already exist? -- yes;
// cent-safe money splitting IS the largest-remainder problem, restated in cents instead of
// percentage points). `alloc_weighted(100, values)` treats the series' own values as weights; a
// tied 3-way split of equal weights lands as `[34, 33, 33]` (traced through the algorithm, not
// assumed -- the KAT asserts the exact list, plus two more awkward splits). An all-zero series
// (every weight 0) is `alloc_weighted`'s own already-handled edge case: it falls back to
// `alloc_equal`, an even split, instead of dividing by a zero weight-total.
//
// ── SPARKLINE: A FLAT SERIES MAPS TO Minus(), THE SAME "NEUTRAL" READING StatFlat ALREADY GIVES IT
// Each point is classified against the SERIES' OWN [min, max] range: `Check()` ("at or above the
// midpoint") or `Minus()` ("below it") -- the identical binary vocabulary `_prism_in_rating_star`
// already established for "no star glyph exists, reuse check/minus". `pct = ((point - min) * 100)
// / (max - min)` is guarded when `max == min` (every point identical, so there is no meaningful
// position within a zero-width range) -- instead of dividing by zero, every point renders
// `Minus()`, mirroring `prism_stat_trend_flat`'s own choice of `Minus()` for "flat, nothing to
// report" (prism_ui_data.nova).
//
// ── FIELD PREFIX: ONE SHARED ITEM TYPE FOR BAR, PIE, AND LEGEND ──────────────────────────────
// `PrismChItem` is ONE record shape for all three (each is "a label paired with an integer value")
// rather than three near-identical structs with three near-identical prefixes -- `ch_item_*` is
// the single collision-safe prefix all three need (NOVA's field-name -> slot table is GLOBAL,
// last-registration-wins).
//
// PUBLIC API
//   PrismChItem { ch_item_label: string, ch_item_value: int } + prism_ch_item(label, value)
//   prism_ch_bar(title: string, series: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
//     series: list<PrismChItem>. rejects: empty title, empty series, a non-PrismChItem element, a
//     negative value, a duplicate series label. An all-zero series renders every bar fully empty
//     (never divides by zero).
//   prism_ch_sparkline(points: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
//     points: list<int>. rejects fewer than 2 points, a non-int element. A flat series (every
//     point equal) renders every point Minus() (never divides by zero).
//   prism_ch_pie(title: string, series: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
//     series: list<PrismChItem>. Same rejections as bar. Percentages sum to exactly 100 via
//     largest-remainder apportionment (std/money/allocate.nova, reused not reimplemented).
//   prism_ch_gauge(label: string, value: int, min_val: int, max_val: int) -> Result<PrismNode>
//     rejects min_val >= max_val, value outside [min_val, max_val], an empty label (propagated
//     from prism_range).
//   prism_ch_legend(series: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
//     series: list<PrismChItem>. Same rejections as bar/pie. Built with
//     prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_kv (itself built on prism_ui_collect) -- never a hand-rolled loop.

import prism_node
import prism_arrange
import prism_content
import prism_interact
import prism_structure
import prism_ui_kit
import std/money/allocate as alloc

// ── Shared series-item type (bar, pie, legend) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
type PrismChItem
    ch_item_label: string
    ch_item_value: int

fn prism_ch_item(label: string, value: int) -> PrismChItem
    PrismChItem(label, value)

// Type + non-negativity + duplicate-label check, shared by bar/pie/legend. See header: this is
// the FIRST and only check for pie/legend (neither routes through prism_grid/prism_each); bar gets
// a second, redundant "duplicate row key" rejection from prism_grid itself, never actually reached
// because this one runs first.
fn _prism_ch_check_items(items: list) -> Result<int>
    let seen = {}
    let mut idx = 0
    for it in items
        if type_name(it) != "PrismChItem"
            return err("prism_ch: series item " + str(idx) + " is not a PrismChItem (got " + type_name(it) + ")")
        if it.ch_item_value < 0
            return err("prism_ch: series item '" + it.ch_item_label + "' has a negative value (" + str(it.ch_item_value) + ")")
        if it.ch_item_label in seen
            return err("prism_ch: duplicate series label '" + it.ch_item_label + "'")
        seen[it.ch_item_label] = true
        idx += 1
    ok(idx)

fn _prism_ch_max(items: list) -> int
    let mut m = 0
    for it in items
        if it.ch_item_value > m
            m = it.ch_item_value
    m

fn _prism_ch_weights(items: list) -> list
    let out = []
    for it in items
        out.push(it.ch_item_value)
    out

fn _prism_ch_pcts(items: list) -> list
    alloc.alloc_weighted(100, _prism_ch_weights(items))

// ── Bar ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
let PRISM_CH_BAR_TRACK = 10

fn _prism_ch_track_idxs() -> list
    let out = []
    let mut i = 0
    while i < PRISM_CH_BAR_TRACK
        out.push(i)
        i += 1
    out

// See header: guarded to 0 when max_value == 0 (only possible when every value is 0).
fn _prism_ch_bar_width(value: int, max_value: int) -> int
    if max_value == 0
        return 0
    (value * PRISM_CH_BAR_TRACK) / max_value

fn _prism_ch_bar_glyph(idx: int, width: int) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if idx < width
        return prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_content.prism_icon_check())
    prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_content.prism_icon_minus())

// prism_grid's cell_fn contract: (row_item, column) -> Result<PrismNode>.
fn _prism_ch_bar_cell(item, column: string, max_value: int) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if column == "label"
        return prism_content.prism_label(item.ch_item_label)
    if column == "value"
        return prism_content.prism_label(str(item.ch_item_value))
    let width = _prism_ch_bar_width(item.ch_item_value, max_value)
    let mk = fn(idx) _prism_ch_bar_glyph(idx, width)
    let cells = prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_collect(_prism_ch_track_idxs(), mk)?
    prism_arrange.prism_band(cells)

fn prism_ch_bar(title: string, series: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if title == ""
        return err("prism_ch_bar: title must not be empty")
    if len(series) == 0
        return err("prism_ch_bar: needs at least one series entry")
    _prism_ch_check_items(series)?
    let max_value = _prism_ch_max(series)
    let title_node = prism_content.prism_label(title)?
    let key_fn = fn(it) it.ch_item_label
    let cell_fn = fn(it, col) _prism_ch_bar_cell(it, col, max_value)
    let body = prism_structure.prism_grid(series, key_fn, ["label", "bar", "value"], cell_fn)?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([title_node, body])

// ── Sparkline / line ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// See header: Check() at/above the range midpoint, Minus() below it (or the whole series, flat).
fn _prism_ch_spark_level(point: int, min_v: int, max_v: int) -> bool
    if max_v == min_v
        return false
    let pct = ((point - min_v) * 100) / (max_v - min_v)
    pct >= 50

fn _prism_ch_spark_glyph(point: int, min_v: int, max_v: int) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if _prism_ch_spark_level(point, min_v, max_v)
        return prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_content.prism_icon_check())
    prism_content.prism_glyph(prism_content.prism_icon_minus())

fn prism_ch_sparkline(points: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(points) < 2
        return err("prism_ch_sparkline: needs at least 2 points, got " + str(len(points)))
    let mut idx = 0
    for p in points
        if not is_int(p)
            return err("prism_ch_sparkline: point " + str(idx) + " must be an int, got " + type_name(p))
        idx += 1
    let mut min_v = points[0]
    let mut max_v = points[0]
    for p in points
        if p < min_v
            min_v = p
        if p > max_v
            max_v = p
    let mk = fn(p) _prism_ch_spark_glyph(p, min_v, max_v)
    let glyphs = prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_collect(points, mk)?
    prism_arrange.prism_band(glyphs)

// ── Pie / share ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
fn _prism_ch_pie_row(text: string) -> Result<PrismNode>
    prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_icon_text(prism_content.prism_icon_check(), text)

fn prism_ch_pie(title: string, series: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if title == ""
        return err("prism_ch_pie: title must not be empty")
    if len(series) == 0
        return err("prism_ch_pie: needs at least one series entry")
    _prism_ch_check_items(series)?
    let pcts = _prism_ch_pcts(series)
    let texts = []
    let mut i = 0
    for it in series
        texts.push(it.ch_item_label + " " + str(pcts[i]) + "%")
        i += 1
    let title_node = prism_content.prism_label(title)?
    let mk = fn(t) _prism_ch_pie_row(t)
    let rows = prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_collect(texts, mk)?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([title_node, ...rows])

// ── Gauge ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// See header for why this calls prism_range directly instead of prism_fb_progress.
fn prism_ch_gauge(label: string, value: int, min_val: int, max_val: int) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if min_val >= max_val
        return err("prism_ch_gauge: min (" + str(min_val) + ") must be < max (" + str(max_val) + ")")
    if value < min_val or value > max_val
        return err("prism_ch_gauge: value (" + str(value) + ") must be within [" + str(min_val) + ", " + str(max_val) + "]")
    let track = prism_interact.prism_range(label, min_val, max_val, 1, value)?
    let pct = ((value - min_val) * 100) / (max_val - min_val)
    let text_node = prism_content.prism_label(label + " " + str(pct) + "%")?
    prism_arrange.prism_stack([text_node, track])

// ── Legend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Built with prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_kv, itself built on prism_ui_collect (prism_ui_kit.nova) --
// never a hand-rolled node-building loop here.
fn prism_ch_legend(series: list) -> Result<PrismNode>
    if len(series) == 0
        return err("prism_ch_legend: needs at least one series entry")
    _prism_ch_check_items(series)?
    let pcts = _prism_ch_pcts(series)
    let pairs = []
    let mut i = 0
    for it in series
        pairs.push([it.ch_item_label, str(pcts[i]) + "%"])
        i += 1
    prism_ui_kit.prism_ui_kv(pairs)
